    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryson Stott** (72.63) stands as our premier play. Facing Miles Mikolas, **Bryson Stott** benefits from a massive 13% boost in his dynamic platoon projection, and the combination of a favorable hitter's park and the SP's vulnerability makes him an essential anchor in our 5x5 build. Similarly, **Lawrence Butler** (69.61) offers elite upside; despite a minor park penalty, he projects to capitalize against Tyler Mahle due to significant platoon leverage and favorable wind conditions that favor his power profile. **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.13) and **Daulton Varsho** (63.55) round out the top tier of our starting lineup, both elevated by strong platoon splits and favorable SP matchups that position them as high-efficiency starters for category production.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved the marginal start vs. bench calculus for **Jung Hoo Lee** (47.99), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Jung Hoo Lee** possesses the contact profile we covet, the optimizer favored **Jeremiah Jackson** (49.02) and **Masyn Winn** (48.62) slightly due to their situational batting order placement and the need to preserve our season-long game caps. We are also monitoring **Cal Raleigh** (49.29) and **Luis Arraez** (54.38) closely; both are currently subject to \"Lineup Pending\" status. While **Luis Arraez** carries a 5% boost from wind blowing out, the 7% penalty against Gage Jump keeps his ceiling suppressed. We are operating with high caution regarding **Cal Raleigh**\u2014his sub-50 score is heavily impacted by the difficulty of opposing starter Braxton Ashcraft, making him a potential candidate for a quick sub if official lineups reveal an unfavorable shift in order.\n\nFinally, we must remain vigilant regarding the risk profile of our bottom-third roster spots. **Gavin Sheets** (48.86) and **Matt Chapman** (48.15) occupy marginal territory, with the latter hampered by a negative order adjustment and an unfavorable platoon matchup against Jump. We have ruled out any possibility of utilizing **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (0.00) while he remains on the IL, and we are holding **Jonathan Aranda** and **Drew Gilbert** in reserve, as their current efficiency projections do not justify displacing our high-SB upside starters like **Tyler Freeman**. If weather patterns shift in the later games, we may pivot to protect our cap, but as of now, this lineup represents our most statistically sound path toward maintaining our edge in SB and counting stats.",
